James Rising seeks to develop a smart tool-using system for AI responses and shared a conversation example. He asked for guidance on the behavior of an AI model (Arachne) when initially it chooses to perform `web.search` instead of using previously provided URLs to fetch information about individuals on a visit list. The assistant analyzed the situation, identifying tool-selection ambiguity and a lack of structured prior URLs as key issues. It recommended implementing explicit tool-routing rules prioritizing `fetch.url` for known URLs, proper structuring of references, and improved tool descriptions. The assistant emphasized that the model’s behavior was appropriate given its instructions and suggested methods to enhance routing for future requests.
